==Rules==
{{ColosseumRule|Grand Battle}}

==Battleground==
*3 [[Mooth]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 53.33~60 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,800f</sup>.
*2 [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 36.67 seconds<sup>1,100f</sup>, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
*1 [[Bun Bun Black]] spawns after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*2 [[Mr. Mole]]s spawn after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>, delay 113.33 seconds<sup>3,400f</sup>.
*30 [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Bun Bun Symbiote]] spawns after 86.67 seconds<sup>2,600f</sup>.
*4 [[Li'l Bun Bun]]s spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 66.67~73.33 seconds<sup>2,000f~2,200f</sup>.
*1 [[J.K. Bun Bun]] spawns after 133.33 seconds<sup>4,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
You want to kill the 1st enemy ASAP to acquire enough money to deploy your absurdly overpriced Ubers. Bring lots of meatshields, since the enemies combined deal immensely high DPS—cheap meatshields are preferred. Units with high pierce such as [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]], [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]], and [[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|Master of Logic Newtone]] help with semi-reliably juggling Mr. Mole. You'll want to include a counter to Wild Doge in your lineup, since he's one of the most immediate problem-peons; something like [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] or [[Ancient Egg: N112 (Rare Cat)|Cat Egg Pod]] will do.

